\subsection{Phenomenological Implications}

The non-equidistant KK spectrum produces distinct multi-TeV resonances in
di-lepton, di-photon, and di-jet channels. The anharmonic mass shifts modify
production cross sections, decay widths, and branching fractions. The resulting
resonance patterns differ significantly from those predicted by RS models.

