\subsection{Theoretical Consistency}

The STME-RS-A framework remains consistent with:
\begin{itemize}
\item five-dimensional Einstein equations,
\item boundary conditions on UV and IR branes,
\item orthonormality of KK wavefunctions,
\item perturbative stability for $\lambda_4 \lesssim 0.15$,
\item collider constraints for BP1--BP4.
\end{itemize}

The anharmonic deformation does not introduce ghosts or tachyons and preserves
the Sturm--Liouville structure of the KK tower.

\subsection{Future Directions}

Several extensions of the STME-RS-A framework merit further study:
\begin{itemize}
\item inclusion of bulk gauge fields with anharmonic potentials,
\item fermion localization with mode-dependent bulk masses,
\item cosmological implications of anharmonic extra dimensions,
\item KK dark matter candidates from higher modes,
\item FCC-hh and muon collider sensitivity studies.
\end{itemize}

These directions may reveal additional signatures of anharmonic geometry and
provide further opportunities for experimental validation.

